{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>And all the land of Egypt was famished.</b> For the grain they had stored apart from Joseph's had dried out." "<b>Whatever he says to you, you shall do.</b> Because Joseph would tell them to circumcise, and when they came to Pharaoh and said: 'Thus he says to us,' he said to them: 'And why did you not hoard grain? Did he not proclaim to you that years of famine are coming?' They said to him: 'We gathered much and it dried out.' He said to them: 'If so, whatever he says to you, you shall do — he decreed upon the grain and it dried out; what if he decrees upon us and we die!'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:05.528380499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}